 =====================================
 
 a) Concrete behavior and trace
-   - The original task moves a solid n×n square to another solid n×n square through a
-     river of full n×n windows. Here the moving body is an oriented L polyomino inside
-     an n×n bbox, with n in {3,4}. The source component has one extra same-colored tip
-     pixel attached on one occupied side of the L. Removing that tip yields the real
-     moving body.
-   - The tip is not decorative. It gives the unique initial motion direction and is also
-     reused as the docking orientation cue: the red target is a dock frame whose mouth is
-     on the same side named by the tip direction, and whose blue cavity is the same L
-     silhouette as the mover body.
+   - Original task: a solid n x n square moves through blue space, and destination is another
+     solid n x n square. Reachability depends on whether every cell of the translated square
+     stays inside the blue corridor.
+   - Fused variant:
+     1. The mover body is an L polyomino inside an n x n bbox, with n in {2,3,4}.
